# TapTalk — What & Why

Read this before making any change.

**TapTalk** is an iOS16+ (not ios26) AAC (Augmentative & Alternative Communication) app — one place to communicate, plan the day, and use simple daily tools. Built for clarity and accessibility.

**Stack:** React Native · Expo SDK 54 · Expo Router · TypeScript · iPhone first (Expo Go) · EAS

**Core features we are building:**
- **Talk** — AAC board (Mulberry symbols + TalkBoard keyboard) with speech
- **My Day** — daily routine / planning
- **First-Then** — 2-slot visual schedule
- **List** — lists with reminders
- **Goal Tracker** · **Therapeutic Activities** · **Resource Library**

**Core Important Rules:**

- Do NOT **Halucinate**, Meaning do NOT. Make any changes if i didnt mention it or tell you to do it.
- You are able to **Suggest** me other options, If i tell you to do A. You can tell me this is B. and i think it's better (##why...##). Then give me a choice A. Or B. 
- Always ask questions, The more you know the more real the app becomes as you know it more by asking **Questions**.

**Where we are:** Phase 2 — building the iPhone app in code. iPad and App Store come later.

**Repo:** https://github.com/CavenLink-Dev/TapTalk.v2
